statement=(
 'For any finite uniform Boolean f and physical query i, pair real Fourier coefficients a_T,b_T and put pbar_T=a_T^2+b_T^2, s_T=a_T*b_T/pbar_T on positive rows, eta=Inf_i(f), theta=min(eta,1-eta), V=sum pbar_T*s_T^2. '
 'For every normalized reference Q supported on the squared Fourier source support, let qbar be its erasure, t=sum qbar_T*s_T and require both coherent reference outcomes r=(1/2+t,1/2-t) positive. '
 'Then E_pbar s=0, V<=eta(1-eta), and t^2<=chi2(qbar||pbar)*V. If qbar>=beta*pbar for0<beta<=1, its outcome invoice O=D(fair||r) is at most2chi2(qbar||pbar)eta(1-eta)/[beta(2-beta)ln2]. '
 'If also qbar<=Lambda*pbar, replace chi2 by(Lambda-1)(1-beta). For0<theta<=1/2, D(qbar||pbar)>=2|t|log2(1/theta)-log2(5). Hence if D(Q||P)<=B and the same floor holds, O<=[B+log2(5)]^2/[2beta(2-beta)ln2*log2(1/theta)^2]; eta=0,1 give O=0. '
 'The inverse-square-log order is sharp for actual Boolean G_r=epsilon atx0 and (-1)^z(1-2*1{w=0 or(j=1,w=e0+e1)}) atx1, r>=3. Lift the balanced-core q_alpha=(1-alpha)P+alpha delta_full by copying the actual controller-only half and two active data copies; physically query j, normalize inherited references by their own outcomes and refresh both children to SAME-alpha remaining-full laws. '
 'At alpha=1/r, reverse KL tends to0, forward KL tends to1 and is<=2, the likelihood floor is>=2/3, but signed reset sigma~9/[200ln2*r^2] and sigma/Inf_j(G)~9*2^r/[100ln2*r^2] diverges. '
 'At alpha=1/r^2 BOTH KL directions tend to0 (reverse~1/[2ln2*r^2], forward~1/r), while sigma~9/[200ln2*r^4] and sigma/Inf_j(G)~9*2^r/[100ln2*r^4] diverges. '
 'In both profiles all five specified positive posterior credits E,J,P,Gamma,TC keep asymptotics9r4^-r,(1+c)2^-r/2,r2^-r/2,g*r2^-r,1.5r^2*2^-r, with c=18-5log2(10),g=1-1.5log2(1.5), and each divided by sigma or H(G)->2 tends to0. '
 'At alpha=1/r^2 the two reference KL directions also vanish relative to H(G), but are not asserted to vanish relative to sigma. Erased chi2 is exactly alpha^2(1/(10*4^-r)-1)/2 and diverges. This refutes even vanishing two-way KL plus a fixed likelihood floor as a sufficient uniform local reset/influence price. No FEI counterexample, universal initial source price or repeated-reset funding is asserted.'
)
